# Citation metadata for GateLab. Zenodo reads this file (and .zenodo.json) when a GitHub release
# is archived, and GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from it. Keep `version` and
# `date-released` in step with the release being cut.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GateLab, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GateLab"
version: 0.9.2
date-released: "2026-10-14"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23357941
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22787965
    description: "The concept DOI: every version of GateLab."
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23357941
    description: "GateLab 0.9.2."
repository-code: "https://github.com/david-priest/GateLab"
url: "https://david-priest.github.io/GateLab/"
abstract: "Browser-based manual gating of flow and mass cytometry data, with the cell images of the BD FACSDiscover S8 imaging sorter. FCS files are parsed, transformed and gated locally; one population tree per workspace, tailored per file or per group; FlowJo workspace and FACSChorus import and export; Gating-ML 2.0; compensation; statistics and publication figures. The S8's cell images are decoded from its waveform files in the browser, shown on the plot and on an image wall, and counted and measured into channels that can be gated."
keywords:
  - flow cytometry
  - mass cytometry
  - imaging flow cytometry
  - BD FACSDiscover S8
  - CyTOF
  - manual gating
  - Gating-ML
  - FCS
  - FlowJo
authors:
